Retries a rate-limited request at once when its Retry-After or
X-RateLimit-Reset time has already passed. The retry interval was the retry
time minus now, unclamped, so a past time gave a negative interval, and the
libuv timer converts it to an unsigned millisecond count and never fires.
Retry-After: 0 hits this whenever the clock crosses a second between parsing
the response and scheduling the retry
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/actions/runs/42117577416/job/127561385076).
Upstream: not proposed

